1
00:00:08,730 --> 00:00:23,930
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:02,570 --> 00:02:06,570
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION.

3
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:28,230
Are Constantinopolis' treasures are not enough
that you came all this way for treasure?

4
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:31,160
Don't talk too much, woman!

5
00:02:48,230 --> 00:02:50,250
Don't touch her!

6
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:33,900
My Bey...

7
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:38,880
... neither Dündar Bey, nor
Gündüz Bey would let this go.

8
00:03:44,620 --> 00:03:50,940
Brother Boran! Everyone, every
person in this Tent will know this.

9
00:03:52,660 --> 00:03:57,600
Whoever betrays Osman,
son of Ertuğrul Gazi...

10
00:03:58,490 --> 00:04:00,530
... their end would be like this.

11
00:04:00,970 --> 00:04:05,090
If I had kept my silence
after this treason today...

12
00:04:05,110 --> 00:04:09,360
... how could I walk in here,
calling myself a soldier, an Alp?

13
00:04:11,190 --> 00:04:14,120
If I hadn't punished
my uncle's son, Batur...

14
00:04:14,730 --> 00:04:17,850
... my own kin...

15
00:04:18,290 --> 00:04:22,920
... If I separate traitors as
"ours" or "theirs" tomorrow...

16
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:26,530
... would my father's efforts and...

17
00:04:27,590 --> 00:04:30,160
... my mother's milk be halal?

18
00:04:31,610 --> 00:04:33,220
- You are right
- You are right, my Bey.

19
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:37,300
We'd give our lives for
your justice, for your way.

20
00:04:40,090 --> 00:04:42,390
Now, what are we going to do, my Bey?

21
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:47,750
I didn't spill all this
blood for nothing, Konuralp.

22
00:04:48,550 --> 00:04:55,260
If anyone, not just my brother or my uncle,
stands in our way, they will share the same fate.

23
00:04:59,590 --> 00:05:02,890
Everyone will be sure of it.

24
00:05:04,460 --> 00:05:09,110
- My son, my valiant.
- He tried to kill me, mother.

25
00:05:09,950 --> 00:05:14,390
- He wanted me dead.
- Nothing's going to happen to you, my valiant.

26
00:05:14,390 --> 00:05:18,870
Don't you worry, your mother's
blessed hands will make you better.

27
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:24,100
He wanted to kill me,
mother, he tried to kill me.

28
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:27,870
Bring those clothes now, Burçin!

29
00:05:31,060 --> 00:05:33,540
Will my brother be okay, mother?

30
00:05:33,630 --> 00:05:37,630
The fate of a Kayı woman is determined
with blood. This is no time to cry.

31
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:40,440
Take these clothes and wash them.

32
00:05:41,290 --> 00:05:44,520
Get up, come on! Hurry.

33
00:05:44,960 --> 00:05:50,490
Burçin, pour some hemp milk on the daisy.
And don't forget to boil the giant fennel.

34
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:52,430
I will, mother Zöhre.

35
00:05:52,660 --> 00:05:55,560
Aygül, make an oven here.

36
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:11,930
Blacksmith.

37
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:16,280
You know about the quarrel
with the castle, we are on alert.

38
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:20,670
I also commanded men to
bring their weapons to you.

39
00:06:20,750 --> 00:06:22,970
- Take a look at them.
- Yes, Gündüz Bey.

40
00:06:23,130 --> 00:06:27,830
I don't want laziness in the Tent, you should
know that. Everyone needs to do their job now.

41
00:06:27,890 --> 00:06:30,140
- Yes, my Bey.
- Can I come in my Bey?

42
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:31,270
Come.

43
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:35,520
- Gündüz Bey.
- What? What happened to you?

44
00:06:35,610 --> 00:06:38,210
- Osman Bey.
- What happened to Osman Bey?

45
00:06:38,410 --> 00:06:41,960
Osman bey stabbed Batur
in front of Dündar Bey's tent!

46
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:06,300
Osman, may your hands never hold a shield,
may your chest fill with blood, Osman!

47
00:07:06,450 --> 00:07:09,030
If I become a traitor like your son...

48
00:07:09,730 --> 00:07:13,380
-... may it be like you said, aunt.
- Haven't you got enough blood?

49
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:18,430
Is it my son, Batur's turn, after Aybars?

50
00:07:27,580 --> 00:07:28,890
You know...

51
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:36,230
... we wash life with life, and blood with
blood! Let go of my hand, Gündüz Bey!

52
00:07:36,410 --> 00:07:40,680
Do you want injustice, or justice, aunt?

53
00:07:41,030 --> 00:07:42,860
Let go of my hand.

54
00:07:44,290 --> 00:07:47,510
I want revenge, Gündüz Bey.

55
00:07:47,610 --> 00:07:52,480
Why is your voice so high, Zöhre Hatun?
Aren't there men left in your tent?

56
00:08:01,740 --> 00:08:04,710
This is not over yet, Osman.

57
00:08:05,380 --> 00:08:07,510
You spilled my own blood.

58
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:12,940
If you wanted to take
my son away from me...

59
00:08:13,330 --> 00:08:15,920
... then you will pay for it!

60
00:08:31,290 --> 00:08:34,390
You've done this too, Osman?

61
00:08:36,690 --> 00:08:39,210
You've done this too, at last.

62
00:08:40,310 --> 00:08:42,700
Enough of this, Osman!

63
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:46,360
When will you stand still?

64
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:49,210
When will you calm down?

65
00:08:49,250 --> 00:08:54,280
Your brother will calm down
when the treachery ends, brother!

66
00:08:55,710 --> 00:09:00,250
No, you won't come to your senses, Osman.

67
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:04,820
You won't learn.

68
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:10,230
Alps!

69
00:09:12,570 --> 00:09:15,680
Put Osman Bey in the cage!

70
00:09:29,580 --> 00:09:34,130
Treason, or being a part of treason.

71
00:09:35,190 --> 00:09:38,800
There is no difference for me, Gündüz Bey!

72
00:09:39,630 --> 00:09:44,910
I am obeying the law because you are the
Commander, not because you are my brother.

73
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:51,870
I will confront you for all this too.

74
00:09:53,020 --> 00:09:54,180
You should know that.

75
00:10:19,250 --> 00:10:20,710
My son.

76
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:24,200
My son.

77
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:26,910
My son.

78
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:31,950
Son, fighting like a lion with mane...

79
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:37,060
... when he didn't even have a
mustache as big as his eyebrows.

80
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:40,500
Son, standing up like a banner...

81
00:10:42,690 --> 00:10:45,310
... when he falls.

82
00:10:48,920 --> 00:10:54,120
You made this black earth your home...

83
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:57,230
... oh, my son!

84
00:10:59,370 --> 00:11:04,680
Son, no, you are not dead.

85
00:11:05,180 --> 00:11:11,360
Doesn't the One who created
these lands and the sky say so?

86
00:11:11,740 --> 00:11:17,460
- Surah Al-Baqarah [2:154]
"Rather, they are alive,
but you perceive [it] not."

87
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:22,610
We don't perceive it, son, we don't.

88
00:11:23,190 --> 00:11:24,680
But...

89
00:11:26,170 --> 00:11:30,320
... the ones who will come
after you will know it.

90
00:11:30,900 --> 00:11:32,190
They will know, son.

91
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:36,330
Son, if you don't fall...

92
00:11:37,590 --> 00:11:40,280
... If I don't fall...

93
00:11:40,770 --> 00:11:46,630
... how could this, this black
earth become our homeland?

94
00:11:49,340 --> 00:11:52,080
How could this black earth
become our homeland?

95
00:12:08,550 --> 00:12:11,030
What is it, Erkutalp,
why are you in a rush?

96
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:15,080
My Bey, Osman Bey stabbed Batur
in front of Dündar Bey's tent.

97
00:12:15,130 --> 00:12:19,130
What are you talking about, Erkutalp?
What are you talking about?

98
00:12:29,880 --> 00:12:32,940
Come on, come on! Come on!

99
00:12:53,690 --> 00:12:55,520
Forgive us, my Bey.

100
00:12:57,480 --> 00:13:01,920
- Whatever the command says.
- Everyone should do their duties first.

101
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:07,860
No one should be upset because
of their duties, my brothers.

102
00:14:23,570 --> 00:14:25,470
Bring the goods!

103
00:14:57,710 --> 00:15:00,660
So, you are thirsty. Huh?

104
00:15:02,850 --> 00:15:06,610
You won't even get a sip
of it before you talk.

105
00:15:16,930 --> 00:15:20,820
- Bamsı Bey.
- My Osman!

106
00:15:21,890 --> 00:15:26,060
- Why, my valiant?
- Every treason has consequences.

107
00:15:27,450 --> 00:15:31,730
And Batur paid the consequences
of his treason!

108
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:38,540
Good, good then, he got what he deserved.

109
00:15:38,850 --> 00:15:42,650
But Osman, what is that treason? Tell me.

110
00:15:42,890 --> 00:15:48,780
They handed over Theokoles, the biggest
leverage that would lead us to...

111
00:15:49,180 --> 00:15:53,180
... my brother, Aybar's
killers, to the castle.

112
00:15:55,210 --> 00:15:59,340
Who did this, my Osman,
who could've done this to us?

113
00:16:00,310 --> 00:16:04,370
My uncle, my brother...

114
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:07,430
... Batur.

115
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,100
Whose blood is this?

116
00:16:38,700 --> 00:16:40,530
Whose blood is this?

117
00:16:40,690 --> 00:16:45,400
Osman Bey attacked Batur, my Bey.
Zöhre Hatuns are treating him inside.

118
00:17:12,950 --> 00:17:17,560
Lion of his father, my Batur.

119
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:23,840
You will get better, my
son, you will get better.

120
00:17:26,060 --> 00:17:29,320
He tried to kill me, father.

121
00:17:30,220 --> 00:17:34,220
Osman has spilled our blood.

122
00:17:39,250 --> 00:17:43,800
Where is this Osman hiding now?

123
00:17:44,060 --> 00:17:48,190
- Where is he?
- He is neither hiding nor afraid.

124
00:17:48,590 --> 00:17:54,660
He is Osman, he implied that he
did good, while looking at my eyes.

125
00:17:55,080 --> 00:17:59,980
He will suffer the consequences
of spilling Dündar Bey's son's blood!

126
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:05,350
Father, stop him...

127
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:09,030
... or he will be the end of us.

128
00:18:16,060 --> 00:18:17,800
Dündar Bey!

129
00:18:26,350 --> 00:18:32,770
Gündüz put him in a cage. Being
his uncle is finished now, Dündar Bey.

130
00:18:33,050 --> 00:18:37,050
Let Osman see your Bey
face too from now on.

131
00:18:37,230 --> 00:18:43,410
I will show Osman what is the
meaning of spilling blood now.

132
00:18:47,800 --> 00:18:49,140
I will show him.

133
00:18:55,710 --> 00:19:00,130
What were you doing while
Osman was stabbing my son?

134
00:19:01,210 --> 00:19:02,800
What were you doing?

135
00:19:03,960 --> 00:19:05,320
Dündar Bey!

136
00:19:06,660 --> 00:19:09,960
What were you thinking, Dündar Bey!

137
00:19:19,450 --> 00:19:24,050
How could you give the bait that would
help us find Aybar's killers, Dündar Bey!

138
00:19:24,490 --> 00:19:27,040
How could you hand him over to the castle?

139
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:29,740
So that there won't be any more sorrows.

140
00:19:30,390 --> 00:19:34,870
So that valiants like Aybars won't fall.

141
00:19:36,170 --> 00:19:40,930
So that we don't fight
with the Byzantine while...

142
00:19:41,670 --> 00:19:44,590
... the Mongols try to come at us.

143
00:19:45,690 --> 00:19:52,070
So that we keep our Tent alive
until my brother comes back, Bamsı Bey!

144
00:19:53,850 --> 00:19:58,070
But, what has changed after we did that?

145
00:19:59,100 --> 00:20:05,720
Osman Bey, the great warrior of Kayı,
sneaked inside and killed him anyway.

146
00:20:07,180 --> 00:20:12,800
Open your ears now, Bamsı Bey,
Osman is the one who killed Theokoles!

147
00:20:16,210 --> 00:20:22,300
He almost killed my Batur,
if it wasn't for the people.

148
00:20:24,990 --> 00:20:29,340
He almost ripped my heart out.

149
00:20:29,890 --> 00:20:32,100
He almost ripped my heart out.

150
00:20:32,920 --> 00:20:41,190
Dündar Bey, my Osman's courage, my
Osman's strength has broken your balance!

151
00:20:41,230 --> 00:20:43,970
You blame Osman for everything!

152
00:20:44,820 --> 00:20:53,210
From Yorgopolos' death to Theokoles'
murder, every lead is pointing Osman.

153
00:20:53,720 --> 00:20:58,490
Don't you cast a shadow on Kayı's
future by joining Osman's party!

154
00:20:58,960 --> 00:21:03,600
Open your eyes! See the truth yourself!

155
00:21:04,750 --> 00:21:09,440
Do you know what I see when I open my
eyes and look at you, Dündar Bey?

156
00:21:09,540 --> 00:21:11,880
Do you know what I see?

157
00:21:12,290 --> 00:21:16,290
Laziness, I see laziness
when I look at you!

158
00:21:17,850 --> 00:21:23,720
Not laziness, it's caution,
Bamsı Bey, it's caution.

159
00:21:26,750 --> 00:21:30,390
Bithynia's balance is like scales.

160
00:21:30,610 --> 00:21:37,540
I won't let Osman do as he pleases
and hurt people's lives anymore!

161
00:21:38,330 --> 00:21:40,800
You will see, I won't let him.

162
00:21:41,180 --> 00:21:45,180
Osman is my Ertuğrul Bey's entrusted!

163
00:21:45,580 --> 00:21:49,170
I won't let you touch Osman, Dündar Bey!

164
00:21:49,280 --> 00:21:50,440
I won't let you!

165
00:21:50,730 --> 00:21:54,730
We didn't find this Tent on
a road, Bamsı Bey! I...

166
00:21:54,950 --> 00:21:57,420
... am Dündar, son of Süleyman Şah!

167
00:21:57,970 --> 00:22:01,970
Even if, not even Osman,
my own son who is struggling...

168
00:22:02,370 --> 00:22:06,370
... for his life inside tries
to harm Kayı's future...

169
00:22:07,680 --> 00:22:10,980
... I won't show mercy, I will destroy!

170
00:22:11,710 --> 00:22:15,710
While I, Bamsı Beyrek...

171
00:22:15,990 --> 00:22:21,240
... am alive, no one will ever
be able to touch Osman!

172
00:22:21,870 --> 00:22:25,870
I will swallow fury, Dündar Bey!
I will breathe blood!

173
00:22:26,900 --> 00:22:32,510
I will spit fire, I will burn everywhere,
Dündar Bey! I will burn everywhere...

174
00:22:32,550 --> 00:22:35,100
... everywhere, Dündar Bey!

175
00:22:42,770 --> 00:22:45,260
My Bey, pardon me, an
important event has occurred.

176
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:46,110
What happened?

177
00:22:46,190 --> 00:22:50,840
They attacked the New Bazaar,
my Bey, they slaughtered everyone.

178
00:22:51,350 --> 00:22:55,730
What did you say? Inform Gündüz Bey
at once, we are going to the New Bazaar.

179
00:22:55,780 --> 00:22:58,310
- Now!
- Yes, my Bey.

180
00:23:02,990 --> 00:23:07,860
When I return, I will confront that Osman.

181
00:23:09,280 --> 00:23:11,010
I will.

182
00:24:15,270 --> 00:24:16,750
You get out.

183
00:24:28,410 --> 00:24:33,400
You got your hands bloody today, Osman.

184
00:24:35,490 --> 00:24:40,110
You spilled the blood of
your own kind today, Osman!

185
00:24:43,090 --> 00:24:47,720
Tell me now, what will this lead to?

186
00:24:48,730 --> 00:24:50,910
What will this action lead to?

187
00:24:51,340 --> 00:24:55,340
I spilled the blood that was poisoning
Kayıs from the inside, brother!

188
00:24:58,310 --> 00:25:00,090
This is just a start.

189
00:25:02,910 --> 00:25:07,600
Don't you ever make
a mistake too, from now on.

190
00:25:14,520 --> 00:25:20,190
I am not Batur, Osman.
Did you hear me? I am not Batur!

191
00:25:20,530 --> 00:25:24,530
I will carve the eyes of the man
who draws a sword on me!

192
00:25:26,280 --> 00:25:27,820
Know your place!

193
00:25:28,840 --> 00:25:32,780
Otherwise, I won't say "My brother"...

194
00:25:36,240 --> 00:25:38,490
I won't wait for my father...

195
00:25:40,620 --> 00:25:43,710
... I will rip your heart out
with my own hands, Osman!

196
00:25:43,920 --> 00:25:48,680
Everything is clear, both
blindness and treason!

197
00:25:51,720 --> 00:25:56,060
You should be afraid, not me!

198
00:26:02,880 --> 00:26:04,400
Osman...

199
00:26:05,070 --> 00:26:09,540
... while you were still
crying on your cradle...

200
00:26:10,690 --> 00:26:13,520
... I was learning
politics from my father.

201
00:26:17,560 --> 00:26:21,840
The purpose is what
matters, Osman. That means...

202
00:26:22,880 --> 00:26:27,300
... sometimes various foul plays
are needed for conquest! That means...

203
00:26:28,030 --> 00:26:32,560
... someone naive as you
can't comprehend these games!

204
00:26:37,570 --> 00:26:41,640
Gündüz Bey, New Bazaar has been attacked,
Dündar Bey is calling for you at once...

205
00:26:41,760 --> 00:26:44,080
... they will be going
there with the Alps.

206
00:26:44,540 --> 00:26:45,870
Bala Hatun.

207
00:26:47,980 --> 00:26:49,300
Brother...

208
00:26:50,530 --> 00:26:52,540
... unlock my hands.

209
00:26:54,110 --> 00:26:57,110
So you can put us
in more trouble, Osman?

210
00:26:57,220 --> 00:27:00,860
Unlock my hands! I need to
get to New Bazaar at once!

211
00:27:00,860 --> 00:27:03,040
Tell me that first...

212
00:27:04,200 --> 00:27:08,540
... what is your business in this?
Why do you care about New Bazaar?

213
00:27:08,660 --> 00:27:09,490
Brother!

214
00:27:10,290 --> 00:27:17,190
You first think about how you are going
to protect yourself from that infidel, Kalonoz.

215
00:27:17,930 --> 00:27:22,110
Brother! Brother, unlock my hands!

216
00:27:25,260 --> 00:27:26,510
Unlock me!

217
00:27:29,230 --> 00:27:30,420
Osman...

218
00:27:32,360 --> 00:27:38,790
... you will get out of here
only when I want you to.

219
00:27:41,090 --> 00:27:43,850
- Those chains won't be
unlocked until my father returns.

220
00:27:44,020 --> 00:27:46,280
Brother. Brother!

221
00:28:13,300 --> 00:28:15,530
Do you want to go?

222
00:28:18,120 --> 00:28:22,120
- You will drown in your cruelty!
- Shut your mouth!

223
00:28:24,320 --> 00:28:25,990
Bring wine.

224
00:28:28,690 --> 00:28:33,800
My Allah, you don't put a burden
on us that we can't carry.

225
00:28:35,200 --> 00:28:38,250
Give me the wisdom of our mother Sümeyye.

226
00:28:40,130 --> 00:28:45,420
Let me be a martyr like
she was. Give me strength.

227
00:28:53,500 --> 00:28:57,500
When I saw you weeping by the horse...

228
00:28:58,560 --> 00:29:00,420
... I made a promise to myself.

229
00:29:02,340 --> 00:29:06,610
I said whoever upsets this Hatun...

230
00:29:08,420 --> 00:29:11,200
... is my sworn enemy.

231
00:29:18,760 --> 00:29:21,080
Bamsı Bey, unlock me!

232
00:29:23,090 --> 00:29:29,070
Now, before my rage comes to
you like a storm, unlock these locks.

233
00:29:29,120 --> 00:29:31,690
Then lock yourselves there.

234
00:29:32,020 --> 00:29:36,020
- My Bey?
- Hurry! Do as I say. Hurry.

235
00:29:41,380 --> 00:29:44,190
Thank you, Bamsı Bey.
They attacked New Bazaar.

236
00:29:44,550 --> 00:29:47,700
- We should go there at once.
- We should, my valiant, hurry.

237
00:29:47,820 --> 00:29:48,890
Let us go now.

238
00:29:56,950 --> 00:30:01,990
Brave warriors of Catalonia,
I raise my toast for you!

239
00:30:10,950 --> 00:30:12,870
Don't you have a heart?

240
00:30:14,480 --> 00:30:19,210
- A little water.
- You heard Salvador, no water until you talk.

241
00:30:19,530 --> 00:30:23,200
Do you think you came all this way
from Catalonia to make me talk?

242
00:30:24,110 --> 00:30:28,360
- What are you talking about?
- Come, I will tell you.

243
00:30:29,310 --> 00:30:33,690
Come, you are not afraid
of a woman, are you?

244
00:30:41,460 --> 00:30:45,240
Idiot! Does it matter
if a wolf is a he or a she?

245
00:30:50,230 --> 00:30:54,470
- She's getting away!
- Catch the girl, go after him, quickly!

246
00:30:57,200 --> 00:30:59,710
- Catch her!
- Hurry!

247
00:32:32,410 --> 00:32:33,700
Zöhre Hatun.

248
00:32:36,060 --> 00:32:40,490
Bamsı Bey helped Osman
escape from the cage.

249
00:32:41,550 --> 00:32:45,870
He started causing us trouble
even before one of them ended.

250
00:34:02,370 --> 00:34:06,200
- You are trapped.
- I will rip your heads off!

251
00:34:49,830 --> 00:34:54,250
If you try to escape again,
I will break your neck!

252
00:35:09,750 --> 00:35:11,300
Take her.

253
00:35:45,100 --> 00:35:46,590
Osman Bey.

254
00:35:51,870 --> 00:35:53,410
Tursun Bey.

255
00:35:53,960 --> 00:35:55,920
I was also coming to you.

256
00:35:56,690 --> 00:35:59,060
What happened at the New Bazaar,
Tursun Bey?

257
00:36:05,650 --> 00:36:09,250
Bamsı Bey. He's like a father to me,
he knows everything.

258
00:36:12,820 --> 00:36:16,510
They attacked the New Bazaar and
killed everyone.

259
00:36:19,370 --> 00:36:22,730
- Gonca Hatun is injured.
- What about Bala Hatun?

260
00:36:26,150 --> 00:36:27,870
Did something happen to her?

261
00:36:29,710 --> 00:36:31,820
They kidnapped Bala Hatun.

262
00:36:39,830 --> 00:36:41,200
Did they do it?

263
00:36:41,200 --> 00:36:43,550
It's certain who made them do it,
Osman Bey.

264
00:36:44,410 --> 00:36:46,800
But no soldiers left the castle.

265
00:36:47,100 --> 00:36:49,570
They must have found someone to do it.

266
00:36:50,390 --> 00:36:52,110
I don't know who they are.

267
00:36:53,950 --> 00:36:56,170
They probably took her somewhere hidden.

268
00:36:58,710 --> 00:37:04,380
I can't go back to the castle. Once Sofia
sees Bala Hatun, she'll see our connection.

269
00:37:04,850 --> 00:37:07,370
Because she saw Bala Hatun and me
together.

270
00:37:10,330 --> 00:37:14,090
From now on, I'm with you, Osman Bey.

271
00:37:14,610 --> 00:37:18,390
We can only save Bala Hatun from those
killers together.

272
00:37:27,010 --> 00:37:29,430
You'll go to the castle, Tursun Efendi (Mister).

273
00:37:30,800 --> 00:37:34,280
- Why, Bey?
- If they wanted to kill Bala Hatun...

274
00:37:34,280 --> 00:37:36,560
... they would do it in the New Bazaar.

275
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:41,340
They will want to torture
and question you.

276
00:37:42,470 --> 00:37:49,460
After they can't get any answers from you,
they'll take you to Bala.

277
00:37:54,860 --> 00:37:57,290
Thank you, my Bey. Thank you.

278
00:37:57,360 --> 00:38:00,490
And we will walk all over them.

279
00:38:02,940 --> 00:38:05,060
- Boran.
- Yes, my Bey?

280
00:38:05,080 --> 00:38:09,730
Tursun Efendi will take us to Bala Hatun.

281
00:38:11,210 --> 00:38:15,210
You go after them with Konuralp.
And we...

282
00:38:15,590 --> 00:38:18,730
... will wait for the news at Sergeant
Samsa's Tent.

283
00:38:18,900 --> 00:38:20,790
Your wish is my command, my Bey.

284
00:38:59,640 --> 00:39:02,800
Tell me such things that...

285
00:39:03,780 --> 00:39:05,950
... will make my anger not crumble you.

286
00:39:11,990 --> 00:39:16,770
When they attacked my bazaar in
broad daylight...

287
00:39:17,720 --> 00:39:20,090
... what were you doing, huh?

288
00:39:20,940 --> 00:39:22,710
What were you doing?

289
00:39:23,260 --> 00:39:26,700
There were a lot of them, my Bey. They
came out of nowhere.

290
00:39:31,990 --> 00:39:35,480
Coming out of nowhere, is this.

291
00:39:44,260 --> 00:39:47,510
Are you scarecrows?

292
00:39:49,470 --> 00:39:53,470
Are your swords there just to show off?

293
00:40:06,770 --> 00:40:10,770
Why do I feed you?

294
00:40:15,270 --> 00:40:16,770
Why?

295
00:40:17,960 --> 00:40:19,690
Why?

296
00:40:28,380 --> 00:40:32,120
If you don't pay your dues to the food
going down your throat...

297
00:40:32,120 --> 00:40:34,540
... you don't need a throat.

298
00:40:56,410 --> 00:40:59,750
You were asking the other day...

299
00:41:00,290 --> 00:41:05,310
... my Bey, what is your favourite smell?

300
00:41:07,060 --> 00:41:09,160
My bey...

301
00:41:12,110 --> 00:41:15,690
Now I'll answer, Nizamettin Efendi.

302
00:41:25,100 --> 00:41:27,290
The smell of blood.

303
00:41:30,980 --> 00:41:32,560
Don't drop your head.

304
00:41:33,720 --> 00:41:39,350
Now I will ask, and you'll answer.

305
00:41:41,240 --> 00:41:42,930
Okay?

306
00:41:43,330 --> 00:41:45,910
As you command, my Bey.

307
00:41:48,590 --> 00:41:53,550
Even dogs bark when they see an intruder.

308
00:41:55,540 --> 00:41:58,500
Did you bark once, Nizamettin?

309
00:41:59,040 --> 00:42:01,490
What happened to this place?

310
00:42:07,130 --> 00:42:10,590
My bey, please.

311
00:42:10,740 --> 00:42:12,700
We made a mistake, forgive us.

312
00:42:18,810 --> 00:42:21,680
Dump these bodies in the forest.

313
00:42:22,950 --> 00:42:26,950
We couldn't benefit from them, maybe the
wolfs and birds will.

314
00:43:01,300 --> 00:43:05,310
Not with your arm Yökberi, you must pull
with your back. Just like that!

315
00:43:18,840 --> 00:43:20,580
Look, son.

316
00:43:21,370 --> 00:43:24,040
This bow is made from maple.

317
00:43:25,400 --> 00:43:28,000
Under the leather, there is buffalo's
bone.

318
00:43:29,100 --> 00:43:31,520
I wrapped the leather myself.

319
00:43:32,690 --> 00:43:34,880
What I'm trying to say is...

320
00:43:37,310 --> 00:43:43,330
Just for your arrow to hit your target,
many beings died.

321
00:43:56,730 --> 00:44:02,640
A man either puts the bow down or hits
his target.

322
00:44:04,230 --> 00:44:08,380
Now, do you wish the take this bow?

323
00:44:59,780 --> 00:45:01,620
Osman Bey.

324
00:45:06,210 --> 00:45:10,130
Bamsı Bey, friends. Welcome.

325
00:45:15,540 --> 00:45:17,270
Thank you.

326
00:45:30,360 --> 00:45:34,090
If you had informed us, I would kill some
goats for you.

327
00:45:34,590 --> 00:45:37,380
You're not late, Sergeant Samsa.

328
00:45:40,010 --> 00:45:41,990
You have honoured my Tent.

329
00:45:43,000 --> 00:45:46,120
Not just sheep and goats, say the word
and all the beings...

330
00:45:46,120 --> 00:45:48,710
... in these lands shall be sacrificed
for you.

331
00:45:52,870 --> 00:45:57,290
But you don't look like you're here for
a feast.

332
00:46:10,250 --> 00:46:13,890
We'll be your guests for a while,
Sergeant Samsa.

333
00:46:14,470 --> 00:46:18,960
Now we can't relax at our own Tent.

334
00:46:23,830 --> 00:46:28,190
Wish for a Tent, it's there. Wish for a
friend, it's here.

335
00:46:28,570 --> 00:46:32,360
Wish for a pavilion, it's right there.
With great pleasure.

336
00:46:36,950 --> 00:46:39,340
Thank you, Sergeant Samsa.

337
00:46:54,810 --> 00:46:57,410
Get well soon, Alişar Bey.

338
00:47:00,530 --> 00:47:03,030
It won't get well anytime soon,
Dündar Bey.

339
00:47:03,990 --> 00:47:10,200
They attacked the banner lord's bazaar,
no one rests from now on.

340
00:47:12,970 --> 00:47:16,060
I'm a hunter in the woods...

341
00:47:16,610 --> 00:47:22,250
... and you, in the battlefield. Tell me,
who could have done this?

342
00:47:25,460 --> 00:47:28,840
It's certain who the enemies are, and who
the brothers are, Alişar Bey.

343
00:47:28,840 --> 00:47:31,690
Only Kulucahisar could do something
like this.

344
00:47:32,230 --> 00:47:36,230
Any such pillaging could only be
done by Kalonoz.

345
00:47:36,360 --> 00:47:41,640
Kalonoz. Let's see who will save you
from me.

346
00:47:49,210 --> 00:47:52,430
Cowards. Cowards.

347
00:48:07,220 --> 00:48:08,890
My sister, are you okay?

348
00:48:15,770 --> 00:48:19,770
Hatun. Hatun are you okay? Hatun(Woman)!

349
00:48:22,830 --> 00:48:25,640
I am Dündar Bey from Kayı Tent.

350
00:48:27,600 --> 00:48:29,950
Osman Bey's uncle?

351
00:48:30,930 --> 00:48:34,550
I'm his brother Gündüz. What happened?
Tell us.

352
00:48:35,900 --> 00:48:39,900
Tell Osman Bey. They killed everyone.

353
00:48:40,270 --> 00:48:42,470
They kidnapped Bala Hatun.

354
00:48:47,340 --> 00:48:51,600
What does that have to do with Osman Bey?
Who is Bala Hatun?

355
00:48:52,620 --> 00:48:56,620
While they killed everyone, why did
they kidnap Bala Hatun?

356
00:48:57,500 --> 00:49:01,500
A merchant's daughter. What does that have
to do with Osman?

357
00:49:07,660 --> 00:49:12,560
Take her to the Tent. Zöhre Hatun
should treat her.

358
00:49:13,230 --> 00:49:15,980
Then I'll come and find everything out.
Come on now.

359
00:49:27,170 --> 00:49:32,830
I'll find everything out, and you'll be
the first one to hear them, Alişar Bey.

360
00:49:34,560 --> 00:49:38,290
Now it's time to go to the castle
and ask questions.

361
00:49:39,120 --> 00:49:43,840
Be prepared, Dündar Bey. Wait for your
banner lord's word.

362
00:49:44,600 --> 00:49:46,700
War is near.

363
00:50:04,150 --> 00:50:09,480
My Bey. Osman Bey ran away from the Tent
with the Alps(Men).

364
00:50:10,090 --> 00:50:11,370
What are you saying?

365
00:50:11,370 --> 00:50:14,280
He wasn't alone. Bamsı Bey went with them.

366
00:50:26,810 --> 00:50:30,670
Don't let her run away again. Or I will
kill you all!

367
00:50:31,930 --> 00:50:34,220
We have visitors!

368
00:51:10,570 --> 00:51:13,650
Princess Sofia. Welcome.

369
00:51:13,880 --> 00:51:17,200
Catalonia's noble Prince Salvador.

370
00:51:18,480 --> 00:51:21,540
I knew you'd do this so easily.

371
00:51:25,930 --> 00:51:27,810
Prince.

372
00:51:43,700 --> 00:51:47,590
-So this is Edebali's daughter Bala.
- She was a hard case.

373
00:51:47,820 --> 00:51:51,430
Efendi Yannis knows how to break that
case open.

374
00:52:52,250 --> 00:52:54,310
Did anything happen, Princess Sofia?

375
00:52:56,750 --> 00:52:58,540
I know her.

376
00:52:59,540 --> 00:53:02,760
I saw her in the castle dressed as
a sister.

377
00:53:05,400 --> 00:53:07,410
The Priest.

378
00:53:10,020 --> 00:53:12,780
She was with Priest Markus.

379
00:53:13,860 --> 00:53:15,600
What does that mean?

380
00:53:18,480 --> 00:53:23,280
Our church's priest was one of them. He
was Edebali's spy.

381
00:53:23,280 --> 00:53:24,770
Damn it!

382
00:53:25,090 --> 00:53:29,220
He's been in the church for two years.
He tricked us all!

383
00:53:29,780 --> 00:53:31,780
How could they do this?

384
00:53:37,630 --> 00:53:40,240
I will kill them all!

385
00:54:00,320 --> 00:54:02,200
Don't you come close!

386
00:54:04,230 --> 00:54:06,130
Or I'll cut her throat.

387
00:54:13,370 --> 00:54:16,830
Let me go, and I'll let her go.

388
00:54:37,040 --> 00:54:39,050
Bala.

389
00:54:39,810 --> 00:54:41,800
Let me go.

390
00:54:41,800 --> 00:54:45,300
My name is not Bala. You are mixing me up
with someone else.

391
00:54:45,300 --> 00:54:49,100
I don't know any of you! Get back or I'll
kill her!

392
00:54:49,280 --> 00:54:53,280
Bala let me go! This is my final warning!

393
00:54:53,390 --> 00:54:55,310
I said get back!

394
00:54:59,230 --> 00:55:02,100
Don't you remember me, Bala?

395
00:55:03,020 --> 00:55:06,620
You were disguised as a sister when I
last saw you.

396
00:55:07,940 --> 00:55:10,780
The church's priest was with you.

397
00:55:10,880 --> 00:55:12,790
What kind of trickery is this?

398
00:55:12,960 --> 00:55:15,530
I'm a simple merchant's daughter
in the New Bazaar.

399
00:55:15,530 --> 00:55:18,200
And your father is Edebali.

400
00:55:20,680 --> 00:55:23,300
- Get her!
- Get back!

401
00:55:25,710 --> 00:55:29,210
I don't care about death.

402
00:55:32,930 --> 00:55:35,500
- Don't you do it!
- Salvador!

403
00:55:35,770 --> 00:55:37,480
Do it.

404
00:56:06,730 --> 00:56:09,410
Princess Sofia, are you okay?

405
00:56:10,250 --> 00:56:14,790
Salvador, send this snake to
Efendi Yannis.

406
00:56:16,080 --> 00:56:20,360
- Tell him what happened.
- As you wish, Princess Sofia.

407
00:56:23,140 --> 00:56:26,890
Helen, we're going to the castle.

408
00:56:27,030 --> 00:56:33,600
Let's see what kind of a demon is hiding
under Priest Markus' clothes.

409
00:57:08,840 --> 00:57:10,450
Where am I?

410
00:57:12,250 --> 00:57:14,110
Who are you?

411
00:57:14,780 --> 00:57:17,930
Don't worry, Hatun. Don't worry.

412
00:57:17,930 --> 00:57:20,510
You are in good hands, in Kayı Tent.

413
00:57:21,840 --> 00:57:25,190
You were injured. You passed out at
the bazaar.

414
00:57:25,620 --> 00:57:29,650
May Allah bless you all. You took
the trouble.

415
00:57:29,740 --> 00:57:33,740
At least you're alive. Thankfully.

416
00:57:51,560 --> 00:57:56,150
It's an old mark. Looks like it wasn't
your first fight, Hatun.

417
00:58:09,280 --> 00:58:12,930
- Do you use swords?
- Matter of life.

418
00:58:13,280 --> 00:58:15,270
It makes one do such things.

419
00:58:16,260 --> 00:58:19,190
A pack of monsters attacked us.

420
00:58:19,860 --> 00:58:23,900
- Why did they do this?
- How can you look for a reason in them?

421
00:58:24,710 --> 00:58:27,330
It's obvious that they were out raiding.

422
00:58:29,600 --> 00:58:33,850
We're just merchants in the bazaar.

423
00:58:36,600 --> 00:58:40,900
Put ointment on her leg. It should form
a scab.

424
00:58:41,570 --> 00:58:45,470
Put an Alp(man) on her side. She should
not go anywhere.

425
00:59:23,140 --> 00:59:25,060
Alişar Bey.

426
00:59:27,250 --> 00:59:30,220
Did you attack the bazaar, Princess Sofia?

427
00:59:37,800 --> 00:59:41,580
- Welcome.
- I don't feel welcomed.

428
00:59:41,900 --> 00:59:46,750
Tell me. Did they take the attack
orders from you?

429
00:59:47,690 --> 00:59:49,840
Alişar Bey.

430
00:59:51,130 --> 00:59:57,500
You've lived enough in these lands to know
how sensitive the balance is.

431
00:59:58,820 --> 01:00:02,820
Being ignorant isn't enough to do
such a thing.

432
01:00:03,690 --> 01:00:06,400
You also need to be stupid.

433
01:00:06,980 --> 01:00:09,840
Who did it then?

434
01:00:10,050 --> 01:00:15,460
Who is crazy enough to attack my bazaar
in my land?

435
01:00:15,560 --> 01:00:21,360
Alişar Bey. We don't know who
attacked the bazaar.

436
01:00:22,030 --> 01:00:25,710
You know that we wouldn't do such a thing.

437
01:00:27,590 --> 01:00:31,340
Or is there another reason behind you...

438
01:00:31,340 --> 01:00:39,380
... coming to our castle with your
soldiers, your swords, and threatening us?

439
01:00:40,660 --> 01:00:46,320
Whoever is behind this, the only place
they will run to...

440
01:00:46,320 --> 01:00:47,850
... is their death.

441
01:00:51,560 --> 01:00:57,870
Everyone knows that you're the libra
in these lands, Alişar Bey.

442
01:00:58,670 --> 01:01:05,030
If we're on one side of the scale, Kayı
Tent is on the other side.

443
01:01:06,320 --> 01:01:11,040
Did you threaten them like you
are threatening us?

444
01:01:11,620 --> 01:01:15,670
Dündar Bey heard the news about the
attack after it happened, like me.

445
01:01:16,210 --> 01:01:19,310
Besides, why would they do this?

446
01:01:22,810 --> 01:01:25,330
What about Osman?

447
01:01:27,350 --> 01:01:30,360
Did Osman also hear it after it happened?

448
01:01:33,980 --> 01:01:38,520
No one else could have done this.

449
01:01:40,290 --> 01:01:42,720
Why would Osman do it?

450
01:01:44,350 --> 01:01:47,400
The same reason he killed my father for.

451
01:01:49,280 --> 01:01:53,280
That's all he wants. Ending the peace.

452
01:01:53,890 --> 01:01:58,740
He just wants to create a war in
these lands.

453
01:02:16,070 --> 01:02:20,070
Then there is only one way to find out.

454
01:02:21,030 --> 01:02:25,170
We'll go to the Kayı Tent
together, Princess.

455
01:02:26,950 --> 01:02:28,820
Is Osman there?

456
01:02:29,540 --> 01:02:32,110
Osman is in the cage.

457
01:02:38,250 --> 01:02:44,590
It's time to face the facts. The truth
will rise to the surface.

458
01:02:56,500 --> 01:03:00,910
And when God gives them the punishments
they deserve...

459
01:03:01,850 --> 01:03:05,010
... they will see the reason.

460
01:03:05,680 --> 01:03:09,860
Because they are dragged behind
their desires...

461
01:03:10,950 --> 01:03:14,100
... they won't know what being
a human is about.

462
01:03:20,450 --> 01:03:24,750
What do you think you're doing in God's
home. What are you doing here?

463
01:03:29,230 --> 01:03:33,710
God's home, huh? I could kill you with my
bare hands, old man.

464
01:03:35,040 --> 01:03:36,730
With my bare hands!

465
01:03:47,430 --> 01:03:51,120
What do you want from me? I'm an innocent
priest!

466
01:03:51,120 --> 01:03:53,760
An innocent priest, huh?

467
01:03:55,540 --> 01:03:59,980
This is the end of the road,
Priest Markus.

468
01:04:05,830 --> 01:04:07,590
Take him!

469
01:04:19,900 --> 01:04:23,830
Since the day I got my sword...

470
01:04:24,250 --> 01:04:30,840
... my Rab has given me the chance to
fight the evil ones.

471
01:04:33,490 --> 01:04:38,400
I got old. I won't touch another sword,
I said to myself.

472
01:04:39,910 --> 01:04:44,500
But I got back on my feet with my Osman.

473
01:04:46,580 --> 01:04:51,050
My son, my life, my Aybars...

474
01:04:54,010 --> 01:04:58,010
... drank from the shahada sharbat.
And then...

475
01:04:58,940 --> 01:05:02,940
... my soul rose once again.

476
01:05:05,880 --> 01:05:07,970
Osman.

477
01:05:08,680 --> 01:05:12,070
Son, so glad I have you.

478
01:05:13,090 --> 01:05:18,030
So glad I have you, my dark Osman.
Glad I have you.

479
01:05:23,390 --> 01:05:28,040
For your cause, I sacrifice my pavilion,
my Tent, my life, Osman Bey.

480
01:05:28,600 --> 01:05:32,700
I'll run to your orders. I'll
conquer countries.

481
01:05:33,510 --> 01:05:35,960
I'll demolish walls.

482
01:05:36,030 --> 01:05:39,720
Thank you, Sergeant Samsa. Thank you.

483
01:05:40,140 --> 01:05:44,760
Being a friend of such a valiant like you,
is a crown of manhood.

484
01:05:45,200 --> 01:05:49,520
Let's say we have rescued Bala Hatun...

485
01:05:50,040 --> 01:05:52,340
... what about the nation's situation?

486
01:05:52,760 --> 01:05:56,640
Mongolians are wild monsters. The
evilness of Byzantine won't end.

487
01:05:56,900 --> 01:06:00,040
Disorder will burn the Turkish Tents
to the ground.

488
01:06:00,510 --> 01:06:03,870
Dündar Bey gets angry the moment we talk
about a battle.

489
01:06:03,970 --> 01:06:07,970
The age has changed, the times have
changed, Sergeant Samsa.

490
01:06:09,500 --> 01:06:16,570
Now, we'll be bolts of lightning and
dominate the skies without relaxing!

491
01:06:19,000 --> 01:06:23,000
Our swords will get out of their covers,
not to get in ever again.

492
01:06:28,800 --> 01:06:33,230
Whoever follows their desires, will not
be with us.

493
01:06:34,910 --> 01:06:39,130
We'll always be sharp, we'll always be
fresh.

494
01:06:40,090 --> 01:06:42,930
We'll spill the cruel's blood in such
a way that...

495
01:06:43,740 --> 01:06:47,500
... our names will scare all hearts!

496
01:06:50,940 --> 01:06:56,430
I'm the son of Ertuğrul Gazi, Osman.

497
01:06:58,840 --> 01:07:02,590
I swear on the galloping horses
in my blood.

498
01:07:05,170 --> 01:07:08,130
I'll ignite the resurrection fire.

499
01:07:09,300 --> 01:07:13,300
With that fire, I'll burn snakes...

500
01:07:13,800 --> 01:07:19,560
... the fallen ones, and betrayers.

501
01:07:21,900 --> 01:07:24,260
We'll succeed, brothers.

502
01:07:25,050 --> 01:07:29,880
- We'll succeed, if Allah permits.
- We'll succeed son. If Allah permits.

503
01:07:31,690 --> 01:07:34,010
May we come in, Osman Bey?

504
01:07:34,040 --> 01:07:35,250
Come in.

505
01:07:40,990 --> 01:07:44,860
You were right, my Bey.
They caught Tursun.

506
01:07:45,130 --> 01:07:49,310
They threw him in a dungeon. But Boran
brother in on their necks.

507
01:07:51,110 --> 01:07:56,210
Bala Hatun can't be in the dungeon. They
will take him to the uncles.

508
01:07:57,710 --> 01:08:00,570
We need to make their lives
unbearable tomorrow.

509
01:08:02,670 --> 01:08:08,200
But, I hope Boran doesn't
make any mistakes.

510
01:08:08,960 --> 01:08:13,060
Boran brother will inform us once they
take Tursun there.

511
01:10:09,390 --> 01:10:10,380
You...

512
01:10:12,360 --> 01:10:14,450
are the dervish in New Bazaar.

513
01:10:14,860 --> 01:10:18,530
Your father Edebalı was such a wise man...

514
01:10:18,540 --> 01:10:21,280
that he raised a dervish and made him
a priest.

515
01:10:22,740 --> 01:10:24,700
Look at me, you old man!

516
01:10:25,540 --> 01:10:29,540
My father's name isn't Edebalı
and who's the priest?

517
01:10:29,790 --> 01:10:31,860
What are you talking about?

518
01:10:32,830 --> 01:10:36,100
Do you think we don't have
the belief, intelligence...

519
01:10:36,510 --> 01:10:39,120
and courage that your father
has, Bala Hatun (lady)?

520
01:10:39,370 --> 01:10:41,950
I don't know anyone named Bala Hatun!

521
01:10:43,180 --> 01:10:47,180
You and your father were with Ahi Evran
in Kırşehir in some time.

522
01:10:47,790 --> 01:10:50,610
And I was there to become a dervish.

523
01:10:50,700 --> 01:10:53,000
I know your childhood.

524
01:10:53,760 --> 01:10:59,010
I never forget your beautiful eyes
even thousands of years pass, Bala

525
01:11:02,170 --> 01:11:04,350
You're Yannis.

526
01:11:06,910 --> 01:11:10,910
The one who got Mongols killed!

527
01:11:11,450 --> 01:11:14,500
So your father told everything about me.

528
01:11:14,510 --> 01:11:17,240
I know you, Yannis.

529
01:11:18,280 --> 01:11:22,280
-You won't be able to get what you want.
-Don't be so sure.

530
01:11:23,450 --> 01:11:27,450
I serve you death in this plate.

531
01:11:30,130 --> 01:11:34,130
The poison in red bottle
will weaken you...

532
01:11:34,260 --> 01:11:36,730
and make you tell everything.

533
01:11:36,910 --> 01:11:40,910
Then you'll die slowly.

534
01:11:41,420 --> 01:11:45,420
You'll find your cure in blue
bottle whenever you want.

535
01:11:50,570 --> 01:11:54,010
Then I'll set you free.

536
01:11:56,050 --> 01:12:01,450
Don't make me kill a girl that I've
known since her childhood.

537
01:12:13,570 --> 01:12:14,340
No!

538
01:12:15,130 --> 01:12:16,540
-No!
-Open your mouth.

539
01:12:17,240 --> 01:12:18,520
No!

540
01:12:19,070 --> 01:12:20,190
Open your mouth!

541
01:12:20,880 --> 01:12:22,070
Open it!

542
01:13:26,400 --> 01:13:29,050
You're brave like your owner.

543
01:13:29,100 --> 01:13:30,360
You're fearless.

544
01:13:30,820 --> 01:13:33,230
Don't give up.

545
01:13:36,600 --> 01:13:39,500
I'll save you from that swamp.

546
01:13:56,450 --> 01:13:58,630
-My Osman.
-Bamsı Bey.

547
01:13:59,550 --> 01:14:01,810
Come here please.

548
01:14:13,090 --> 01:14:14,510
My Osman...

549
01:14:14,970 --> 01:14:17,270
you look abstracted.

550
01:14:17,480 --> 01:14:19,320
What are you thinking about?

551
01:14:20,290 --> 01:14:21,780
I think that...

552
01:14:22,930 --> 01:14:26,330
whether Tursun draw those devils...

553
01:14:27,430 --> 01:14:29,160
or not.

554
01:14:31,950 --> 01:14:33,080
Son...

555
01:14:33,470 --> 01:14:34,670
are you thinking about...

556
01:14:35,070 --> 01:14:38,160
Tursun or...

557
01:14:39,460 --> 01:14:41,300
Edebalı's daughter?

558
01:14:45,480 --> 01:14:47,230
Both of them.

559
01:14:47,980 --> 01:14:51,300
They will lead us to those cruels' base.

560
01:14:58,970 --> 01:15:02,970
My brave Osman...

561
01:15:09,380 --> 01:15:10,790
now you...

562
01:15:11,250 --> 01:15:14,590
think it's love?

563
01:15:14,600 --> 01:15:17,500
It's love?

564
01:15:22,000 --> 01:15:23,120
Son...

565
01:15:25,270 --> 01:15:28,250
Do you think land means...

566
01:15:28,460 --> 01:15:32,690
just weapon and shield?

567
01:15:33,290 --> 01:15:37,120
Does it mean gallopers?

568
01:15:38,010 --> 01:15:41,920
My Osman, land doesn't just mean tent...

569
01:15:41,940 --> 01:15:45,020
marquee and fluke?

570
01:15:46,640 --> 01:15:48,350
Land means...

571
01:15:48,950 --> 01:15:50,860
love.

572
01:15:51,890 --> 01:15:53,830
It means longing.

573
01:15:55,880 --> 01:15:57,710
It means lover.

574
01:16:00,100 --> 01:16:03,570
How could they endure the pain...

575
01:16:03,620 --> 01:16:06,160
if Oghuz Khan doesn't have
Yar-Su (a nature layer) and...

576
01:16:06,200 --> 01:16:10,600
if Alparslan doesn't have Selcen and...

577
01:16:10,680 --> 01:16:14,230
if Süleyman Shah doesn't have Hayme?

578
01:16:14,840 --> 01:16:18,840
How could they manage to do big issues?

579
01:16:20,420 --> 01:16:21,930
Son...

580
01:16:22,250 --> 01:16:24,210
men are responsible for their horses...

581
01:16:24,500 --> 01:16:28,500
and the valiant is responsible
for his lover.

582
01:16:33,260 --> 01:16:36,490
May my Allah grant us the best.

583
01:16:36,790 --> 01:16:40,210
In sha Allah, we will dupe them.

584
01:16:40,730 --> 01:16:43,130
Tursun resists the tortures.

585
01:16:43,880 --> 01:16:47,220
He resists and we reach our goal.

586
01:16:49,230 --> 01:16:53,230
May Allah give strength to Tursun.

587
01:16:54,760 --> 01:16:55,920
Amin.

588
01:16:56,290 --> 01:16:57,230
Amin.

589
01:17:10,000 --> 01:17:12,100
No one can save you.

590
01:17:13,020 --> 01:17:15,700
You better start talking.

591
01:17:40,420 --> 01:17:42,820
Even your father can't save you.

592
01:18:10,640 --> 01:18:11,570
Osman...

593
01:18:12,840 --> 01:18:13,970
Osman...

594
01:18:17,150 --> 01:18:18,960
Osman will save me.

595
01:19:11,810 --> 01:19:14,520
Tell me, Priest Marcus.

596
01:19:15,820 --> 01:19:18,420
Or your name is a lie too?

597
01:19:18,540 --> 01:19:22,290
Stop, for the sake of Holy
Mary. I beg you.

598
01:19:22,970 --> 01:19:25,030
What do you want from me?

599
01:19:27,510 --> 01:19:29,430
I'm a priest!

600
01:19:33,880 --> 01:19:36,300
I serve to God.

601
01:19:40,320 --> 01:19:43,010
Ask everyone!

602
01:19:43,770 --> 01:19:45,270
They know me!

603
01:19:54,930 --> 01:19:56,740
You'll kill me!

604
01:19:57,070 --> 01:19:58,550
I beg you. Don't!

605
01:19:59,820 --> 01:20:01,650
-screaming-

606
01:20:07,750 --> 01:20:09,800
-screaming-

607
01:20:44,890 --> 01:20:46,510
Hasn't he talked yet?

608
01:20:46,730 --> 01:20:49,370
He still says he's Priest Marcus.

609
01:20:51,270 --> 01:20:54,060
I can't wait for an answer.

610
01:20:54,530 --> 01:20:57,850
We have to take possession of Holy
Entrustments and the treasure.

611
01:21:33,310 --> 01:21:35,640
I beg you...

612
01:21:37,280 --> 01:21:40,160
for the sake of our Mother Mary, princess.

613
01:21:42,840 --> 01:21:45,550
Pray with me, Priest Marcus.

614
01:21:47,670 --> 01:21:51,820
Hear my prayers for the sake
of Mother Mary.

615
01:21:53,800 --> 01:21:55,340
God...

616
01:21:57,540 --> 01:21:59,600
hear my prayers.

617
01:22:00,740 --> 01:22:02,800
Answer me with your...

618
01:22:04,090 --> 01:22:06,790
loyalty and integrity.

619
01:22:07,880 --> 01:22:10,390
Do not enter into judgment with your servant...

620
01:22:10,910 --> 01:22:13,300
for in Your sight no one...

621
01:22:14,810 --> 01:22:17,360
living is righteous. (Psalm 143:2)

622
01:22:19,130 --> 01:22:21,040
Princess Sofia...

623
01:22:24,200 --> 01:22:26,550
you know me.

624
01:22:29,490 --> 01:22:31,830
Please believe me.

625
01:23:27,820 --> 01:23:29,270
No!

626
01:24:00,160 --> 01:24:02,450
Edebalı raised him well.

627
01:24:06,810 --> 01:24:09,360
Take him to where Bala Hatun is.

628
01:24:12,400 --> 01:24:14,740
Efendi Yannis (Sir) will make them talk.

629
01:24:15,330 --> 01:24:18,170
Do you think he will?

630
01:24:22,880 --> 01:24:25,350
He never talks even if he dies.

631
01:24:30,870 --> 01:24:34,550
But he will...

632
01:24:38,150 --> 01:24:40,220
for Bala Hatun.

633
01:24:59,140 --> 01:25:02,260
-He lost himself.
-He must be very tired.

634
01:25:02,570 --> 01:25:04,830
His wound will tingle when he wakes up.

635
01:25:05,420 --> 01:25:08,710
Then I'll go to the infirmary and take some herbs.

636
01:25:09,300 --> 01:25:12,780
We'll give him when he wakes up.

637
01:25:24,630 --> 01:25:26,220
Where did Aygül go?

638
01:25:26,930 --> 01:25:29,220
To the infirmary, Mother Zöhre.

639
01:25:39,190 --> 01:25:40,910
He's fevered.

640
01:25:42,160 --> 01:25:44,540
He'll get better, Inshaallah.

641
01:26:18,390 --> 01:26:19,280
Burçin.

642
01:26:20,280 --> 01:26:21,890
Come here.

643
01:26:35,400 --> 01:26:39,400
Since your family died in
Mongol trouble...

644
01:26:40,090 --> 01:26:41,940
you've grown up with me.

645
01:26:42,160 --> 01:26:44,610
You know I see you as my child.

646
01:26:45,230 --> 01:26:47,480
And I see you as my mother, Mother Zöhre.

647
01:26:51,380 --> 01:26:55,380
You're closer to Aygül. You're friends.

648
01:26:56,140 --> 01:26:59,560
She's a bit weird these days.

649
01:27:00,290 --> 01:27:04,290
-What's the problem, Burçin?
-Things happened saddened her.

650
01:27:05,910 --> 01:27:07,050
Burçin.

651
01:27:17,250 --> 01:27:19,080
She hesitates to say.

652
01:27:20,040 --> 01:27:23,090
-But I know.
-Know what?

653
01:27:31,290 --> 01:27:34,210
Aygül loves Osman, Mother Zöhre.

654
01:27:35,120 --> 01:27:37,020
She can't say that.

655
01:27:58,690 --> 01:27:59,950
Can I come in?

656
01:28:01,450 --> 01:28:03,220
Come, Sergeant Samsa.

657
01:28:14,850 --> 01:28:16,860
You bring me food.

658
01:28:17,180 --> 01:28:18,860
You sell grapes.

659
01:28:21,050 --> 01:28:23,380
Are you offended, Sergeant Samsa?

660
01:28:28,430 --> 01:28:31,150
Selling grapes is better
than selling friends.

661
01:28:31,920 --> 01:28:33,790
What's your problem?

662
01:28:34,350 --> 01:28:36,890
You wanted me to stop and not to come.

663
01:28:37,290 --> 01:28:38,450
So?

664
01:28:39,680 --> 01:28:41,240
Are you offended?

665
01:28:42,340 --> 01:28:43,680
You helped.

666
01:28:44,140 --> 01:28:45,900
Your duty is over.

667
01:28:47,030 --> 01:28:51,030
If you had another duty,
Osman Bey would say it.

668
01:28:54,920 --> 01:28:56,050
Konur.

669
01:28:57,010 --> 01:28:59,740
You came as guest. Stay like that.

670
01:29:01,490 --> 01:29:03,770
Or I'll kill you.

671
01:29:14,230 --> 01:29:16,440
I'm not like the others.

672
01:29:18,110 --> 01:29:21,690
I'll harm you.

673
01:29:24,660 --> 01:29:27,010
I'll harm your soul.

674
01:29:32,180 --> 01:29:34,520
What are you doing?

675
01:29:35,590 --> 01:29:38,900
Lower your swords!

676
01:29:40,860 --> 01:29:42,900
Look at them.

677
01:29:45,070 --> 01:29:47,240
Look at them!

678
01:29:47,540 --> 01:29:50,430
You're possessed by the demon!

679
01:29:53,700 --> 01:29:57,700
Sons! When the mountains fall apart,
there occurs a plain...

680
01:29:58,860 --> 01:30:02,150
when they come together, there occurs a
chain of mountains!

681
01:30:02,810 --> 01:30:06,810
My Osman, Osman Bey offers to
resurrect.

682
01:30:07,510 --> 01:30:09,510
But you run wild!

683
01:30:11,700 --> 01:30:16,230
Sons, you need to be a friend to my
Osman.

684
01:30:17,210 --> 01:30:18,920
That is why...

685
01:30:19,840 --> 01:30:22,900
you need to be brothers first.

686
01:30:23,640 --> 01:30:24,920
Now...

687
01:30:25,550 --> 01:30:28,710
now give your blessings to each other
and hug.

688
01:30:30,330 --> 01:30:34,670
Hug each other so that your brotherhood
will be renewed.

689
01:30:36,140 --> 01:30:39,630
Hug each other so that we can
destroy the enemy!

690
01:30:44,630 --> 01:30:46,980
- Give me your blessings.
- You too.

691
01:30:49,930 --> 01:30:51,370
Not like that.

692
01:30:52,640 --> 01:30:54,600
This is not enough.

693
01:30:56,360 --> 01:31:01,100
Sons, our prophet (a.s)

694
01:31:01,270 --> 01:31:03,330
What did he say?

695
01:31:03,550 --> 01:31:07,910
The real wrestlers can keep calm...

696
01:31:10,120 --> 01:31:13,300
even when they are angry.

697
01:31:13,300 --> 01:31:19,750
Now, now you shall kiss each other's
hands.

698
01:31:21,140 --> 01:31:24,860
So that you can hold yourself nex time.

699
01:31:24,910 --> 01:31:27,100
Come on.

700
01:31:29,460 --> 01:31:33,030
We almost were going to fight.

701
01:31:33,770 --> 01:31:37,140
We stopped it, my valiant.
Long live.

702
01:31:37,750 --> 01:31:39,850
Oh, Allah.

703
01:31:42,110 --> 01:31:46,160
- Give me your blessings.
- You too, Sergeant Samsa.

704
01:31:46,200 --> 01:31:50,480
Masha Allah (praise) my valiants!

705
01:32:12,040 --> 01:32:13,960
Son.

706
01:32:16,650 --> 01:32:22,100
Being a leader, being Bey is always hard.

707
01:32:39,430 --> 01:32:43,900
If something bad is to happen...

708
01:32:44,640 --> 01:32:48,400
it may strike at the worst time.

709
01:32:48,420 --> 01:32:53,330
Being a Bey needs responsibility.

710
01:32:53,380 --> 01:32:58,020
In situations like this, in a crisis...

711
01:32:59,750 --> 01:33:04,180
How can I start something as being a
Bey?

712
01:33:04,990 --> 01:33:07,540
How can I capture the hearts?

713
01:33:07,620 --> 01:33:11,600
If you want to be a Bey who is reasonable
and kind...

714
01:33:12,000 --> 01:33:17,270
you need to follow Hz. Muhammed...

715
01:33:17,790 --> 01:33:21,500
Sallā Allāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam (Peace be upon him)

716
01:33:24,170 --> 01:33:31,760
Our Master created a new civilization
in spite of all those clans...

717
01:33:32,310 --> 01:33:35,990
in the middle of a desert.

718
01:33:36,050 --> 01:33:40,650
Everyone fell apart, he gathered.

719
01:33:40,650 --> 01:33:45,430
He didn't accept cruelty.
He wasn't afraid of the enemy.

720
01:33:46,110 --> 01:33:50,450
He only wanted justice.

721
01:33:50,520 --> 01:33:54,380
What was justice?

722
01:33:54,380 --> 01:33:55,380
there is no god but Allah and...

723
01:33:56,380 --> 01:33:59,810
...Muhammad is the messenger of Allah

724
01:34:00,620 --> 01:34:04,600
They tried everything to
mislead...

725
01:34:04,780 --> 01:34:07,430
the prophet of mercy.

726
01:34:07,510 --> 01:34:09,490
However...

727
01:34:10,060 --> 01:34:15,670
he said: "even if you give me
the moon and sun...

728
01:34:16,610 --> 01:34:20,330
I still won't give up on my case."

729
01:34:20,470 --> 01:34:27,330
They forced him to stop while he
was trying to help people.

730
01:34:27,330 --> 01:34:31,060
He responded kindly.

731
01:34:31,060 --> 01:34:37,000
In Bedir, Uhud, Hendek, the enemy
went mad.

732
01:34:37,030 --> 01:34:41,850
He beat the cruels to their knees.

733
01:34:44,060 --> 01:34:48,190
He clothed the naked like a night.

734
01:34:48,290 --> 01:34:53,950
He enlighted his era like a oil lamp.

735
01:34:54,910 --> 01:35:00,240
He became a light that spread
all over the world.

736
01:35:00,240 --> 01:35:04,430
He was awake while everyone was sleeping.

737
01:35:04,660 --> 01:35:09,040
Everyone fell, he remained standing.

738
01:35:09,300 --> 01:35:13,300
Everyone was tired, he was the hope.

739
01:35:15,590 --> 01:35:18,300
He was the justice.

740
01:35:18,530 --> 01:35:20,830
He was the compassion.

741
01:35:21,630 --> 01:35:24,560
He was the wisdom.

742
01:35:24,810 --> 01:35:27,660
He was the patience.

743
01:35:29,420 --> 01:35:32,050
You should be someone that
when you walk...

744
01:35:32,860 --> 01:35:36,380
justice walks too.

745
01:35:36,570 --> 01:35:40,240
When you smile, compassion will smile.

746
01:35:41,250 --> 01:35:45,250
When you resist, the
patience will stand up.

747
01:35:45,560 --> 01:35:49,560
And people will find the land in you.

748
01:35:50,630 --> 01:35:55,170
And in this land, the light
of our prophet will seem.

749
01:35:56,360 --> 01:36:01,840
May our Allah will make us a great
ummah to our Prophet.

750
01:36:03,230 --> 01:36:04,490
Amin.

751
01:36:33,090 --> 01:36:34,580
My Allah...

752
01:36:36,770 --> 01:36:38,910
grant me and my people...

753
01:36:40,510 --> 01:36:44,080
to establish an empire that...

754
01:36:45,710 --> 01:36:48,510
will spread the light of our Prophet.

755
01:37:21,950 --> 01:37:25,950
What happened in Kulucahisar in the night
that Governor Yorgopolos died?

756
01:37:29,480 --> 01:37:33,990
You killed Yorgopolos.

757
01:37:34,300 --> 01:37:38,300
He had to die.

758
01:37:38,680 --> 01:37:40,710
We're not killers.

759
01:37:41,040 --> 01:37:45,040
Burn in hell, you devil.

760
01:37:48,600 --> 01:37:51,830
How did you learn that I hid
the Holy Entrustments...

761
01:37:51,980 --> 01:37:55,270
in the Kulucahisar?

762
01:37:55,780 --> 01:37:57,340
You won't learn...

763
01:37:57,590 --> 01:38:01,590
anything from me.

764
01:38:03,150 --> 01:38:06,050
Osman Bey is with Edebalı.

765
01:38:06,510 --> 01:38:10,170
What about Ertuğrul Bey?

766
01:38:10,240 --> 01:38:12,880
Who's in it other than Kayıs?

767
01:38:14,910 --> 01:38:18,890
Neither Osman Bey nor Kayıs...

768
01:38:18,920 --> 01:38:21,290
know about anything.

769
01:38:21,760 --> 01:38:25,090
The night you killed Governor...

770
01:38:25,770 --> 01:38:30,890
he came to where Governor is...

771
01:38:33,490 --> 01:38:36,580
to chase the murderer
of his blood brother.

772
01:38:40,100 --> 01:38:42,050
Calm down.

773
01:38:42,590 --> 01:38:45,490
Calm down. Calm.

774
01:38:55,420 --> 01:38:57,610
Kerem and Aslı.

775
01:39:01,080 --> 01:39:06,230
You try hardly to keep Osman away
from a devil like me.

776
01:39:07,110 --> 01:39:11,110
I see fear in your eyes for him.

777
01:39:13,360 --> 01:39:18,050
Those beautiful eyes says that you're
in love with Osman Bey.

778
01:39:20,210 --> 01:39:23,060
You old man!

779
01:39:25,570 --> 01:39:28,480
I'm telling you the truth.

780
01:39:30,270 --> 01:39:32,250
Osman Bey...

781
01:39:33,020 --> 01:39:35,830
doesn't know our secret.

782
01:39:37,000 --> 01:39:39,190
He doesn't.

783
01:39:39,920 --> 01:39:43,100
So Osman caught up in
it without knowing.

784
01:39:43,120 --> 01:39:46,130
It doesn't matter. He'll die
soon or later.

785
01:39:46,450 --> 01:39:48,550
The Alps (men) in his tent and...

786
01:39:48,550 --> 01:39:53,330
all Turks that occupied
our lands will die!

787
01:39:55,820 --> 01:39:57,700
As to you...

788
01:39:58,350 --> 01:40:00,110
you can live...

789
01:40:00,970 --> 01:40:03,320
if I want to.

790
01:40:04,550 --> 01:40:10,570
Or you'll tell me where the
Holy Entrustments are.

791
01:40:14,200 --> 01:40:15,580
The death...

792
01:40:16,060 --> 01:40:18,880
is our salvation.

793
01:40:21,730 --> 01:40:26,410
Shahada is our meeting.

794
01:40:29,700 --> 01:40:31,950
I'm patient, Bala.

795
01:40:33,360 --> 01:40:36,760
I'll watch you dying.

796
01:40:37,940 --> 01:40:41,310
You'll see that you can't
hide secrets from me.

797
01:40:49,350 --> 01:40:59,100
Bi-smi llāhi r-raḥmāni r-raḥīm ("In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful"

798
01:41:02,380 --> 01:41:11,740
Quran Al-Masad ("The Palm Fiber") [111]
"May the hands of Abu Lahab
be ruined, and ruined is he."

799
01:41:11,900 --> 01:41:21,460
"His wealth will not avail
him or that which he gained."

800
01:41:21,460 --> 01:41:29,940
"He will [enter to] burn in
a Fire of [blazing] flame"

801
01:41:29,940 --> 01:41:37,500
"And his wife [as well]
- the carrier of firewood."

802
01:41:37,500 --> 01:41:47,660
"Around her neck
is a rope of [twisted] fiber."

803
01:42:02,400 --> 01:42:04,000
What did she say, sir?

804
01:42:08,230 --> 01:42:10,540
She prayed.

805
01:42:10,830 --> 01:42:13,780
In the name of Allah, the
Most Beneficent, the Most Merciful.

806
01:42:14,110 --> 01:42:17,950
The hands of Abu Lahab
were ruined, and ruined was he."

807
01:42:18,120 --> 01:42:21,500
He couldn't make use of his wealth
and he didn't gain anything.

808
01:42:21,660 --> 01:42:24,150
He'll go to hell.

809
01:42:24,230 --> 01:42:28,230
Although his wife has a rope
made from twisted fiber

810
01:42:28,300 --> 01:42:32,060
she will go to hell, carrying the firewood.

811
01:42:32,770 --> 01:42:36,920
Her faith won't save her from
my poison. She'll talk.

812
01:43:17,490 --> 01:43:19,350
Sir...

813
01:43:21,700 --> 01:43:24,100
They killed our friends.

814
01:43:25,170 --> 01:43:27,290
We're given out.

815
01:43:43,080 --> 01:43:44,290
Sir...

816
01:43:47,770 --> 01:43:49,710
Bala Hatun...

817
01:43:51,930 --> 01:43:54,180
They abducted her.

818
01:43:59,950 --> 01:44:01,220
My daughter.

819
01:44:03,090 --> 01:44:05,490
Gonca Hatun is wounded.

820
01:44:06,160 --> 01:44:09,690
Dündar Bey took her to Kayı
Tent for the treatment.

821
01:44:10,540 --> 01:44:12,180
Friends...

822
01:44:19,420 --> 01:44:21,850
We aren't counted by fingers...

823
01:44:24,640 --> 01:44:26,960
We aren't given out

824
01:44:29,870 --> 01:44:33,870
For the land, not one child...

825
01:44:34,730 --> 01:44:37,270
but thousand of children are sacrificed.

826
01:44:50,310 --> 01:44:52,730
My Allah who saves İbrahim
from the fire...

827
01:44:53,390 --> 01:44:56,050
İsmail from the knife and...

828
01:44:56,120 --> 01:45:00,120
Yusuf from wellholes, Yunus
in from floods...

829
01:45:01,040 --> 01:45:05,040
and Prophet in caves.

830
01:45:05,680 --> 01:45:09,440
You protect our secret.

831
01:45:10,160 --> 01:45:14,160
Keep my daughter's head up.

832
01:45:15,180 --> 01:45:17,650
Give her strength.

833
01:45:17,870 --> 01:45:21,870
Give her Hz. Ayşe's wisdom...

834
01:45:22,880 --> 01:45:25,650
Hz. Fatima's courage...

835
01:45:26,880 --> 01:45:30,380
and Hz. Sümeyye's patience.

836
01:45:31,100 --> 01:45:35,320
Make us tough against heathens.

837
01:45:36,630 --> 01:45:40,780
Make our weapons strong, make
our horses strong.

838
01:45:42,170 --> 01:45:44,890
Make our valiants victorious.

839
01:45:46,260 --> 01:45:49,840
Make the enemy defeated.

840
01:45:51,060 --> 01:45:55,200
Undoubtfully, victory is yours.

841
01:46:39,310 --> 01:46:41,470
My Bey(chief), they have been trapped.

842
01:46:42,110 --> 01:46:44,030
We got them.

843
01:46:44,140 --> 01:46:46,980
- Where are they?
- They are on the way to Nika.

844
01:46:47,190 --> 01:46:51,170
- Eternal Allah!
- Eternal Allah!

845
01:46:51,190 --> 01:46:53,820
Allah is one!

846
01:47:14,230 --> 01:47:16,300
Hi.

847
01:47:24,970 --> 01:47:27,030
What's the matter, Efendi (sir).

848
01:47:28,210 --> 01:47:33,160
You are a dervish. Why are you checking
weapons?

849
01:47:33,450 --> 01:47:38,800
Carrying a weapon is sunnah.
So, I am doing just like that.

850
01:47:39,210 --> 01:47:41,090
Eyvallah.
(Fair enough)

851
01:47:41,170 --> 01:47:45,520
Also, since Ertuğrul Bey went to Konya...

852
01:47:45,520 --> 01:47:48,240
There has been no peace.

853
01:47:48,330 --> 01:47:53,060
We hear bazaar raids, caravan raids
every day.

854
01:47:53,960 --> 01:47:58,070
You are right Dervish.
Now, there is no peace here.

855
01:47:58,370 --> 01:48:02,370
They raided the new bazaar near the lake
also.

856
01:48:02,570 --> 01:48:07,010
I heard that everybody was killed.
Is this true?

857
01:48:07,030 --> 01:48:11,430
It is true, Dervish.
Their identities are unclear.

858
01:48:11,460 --> 01:48:15,480
- They killed everyone.
- Was there no one left alive?

859
01:48:15,480 --> 01:48:18,550
Just a wounded girl survived.

860
01:48:18,610 --> 01:48:21,660
And Dündar Bey took her to the tent.

861
01:48:23,270 --> 01:48:25,660
How is the Hatun (Lady)?

862
01:48:26,320 --> 01:48:30,770
She is in the infirmary.
Zülha Hatun is taking care of her.

863
01:48:30,770 --> 01:48:36,250
She will be okay, in sha Allah.
But, why are you asking?

864
01:48:36,550 --> 01:48:42,070
Healing comes from Allah, but we can
pray, at least.

865
01:48:51,580 --> 01:49:23,770
O Allah, The healer

866
01:49:23,910 --> 01:49:25,850
O Allah, The healer

867
01:49:29,200 --> 01:49:32,810
O Allah, The healer

868
01:49:32,850 --> 01:49:37,020
O Allah, The healer

869
01:49:37,020 --> 01:49:43,290
In fact, her heal is in my hands.

870
01:49:47,810 --> 01:49:56,740
O Allah, The healer

871
01:52:39,220 --> 01:52:45,960
We could welcome you better if you had
sent a messenger.

872
01:52:45,960 --> 01:52:51,200
We would offer you sherbet and meat
abundantly.

873
01:52:51,310 --> 01:52:55,080
Everybody knows how Kayıs are generous
in the table, Dündar Bey.

874
01:52:55,530 --> 01:53:00,490
We came to talk, not to eat.

875
01:53:12,840 --> 01:53:18,440
You are too crowded for just talking.

876
01:53:19,110 --> 01:53:24,800
However, our home is enough for everyone.

877
01:53:25,160 --> 01:53:27,390
Let's go inside.

878
01:54:35,890 --> 01:54:38,830
Princess Sofia has sent the priest,
Efendi (sir).

879
01:55:00,580 --> 01:55:03,070
What do you want from me?

880
01:55:04,580 --> 01:55:06,470
Who is that girl?

881
01:55:06,530 --> 01:55:11,990
I want you to save this nun, priest.

882
01:55:15,410 --> 01:55:17,490
Which nun?

883
01:55:17,820 --> 01:55:22,950
Look at her face.
Look closer, you'll recognize her.

884
01:55:23,450 --> 01:55:28,130
One of the two nuns who were wandering
with you.

885
01:55:30,670 --> 01:55:34,530
This is a Turkish girl.
Not a nun at all.

886
01:55:34,640 --> 01:55:37,150
What are you looking for?

887
01:55:37,960 --> 01:55:42,070
I don't know this girl.
Just kill her, I don't care.

888
01:55:42,190 --> 01:55:44,390
She is a Turk anyways.

889
01:55:44,480 --> 01:55:50,190
Let me go in the name of god.
You are committing a huge sin.

890
01:56:07,160 --> 01:56:10,930
- What was that?
- Poison.

891
01:56:12,630 --> 01:56:14,620
What are you doing?

892
01:56:17,120 --> 01:56:20,800
This a pill that makes her talk about
everything she knows.

893
01:56:21,110 --> 01:56:27,880
If she doesn't talk, a slow and painful
death is waiting for her.

894
01:56:30,280 --> 01:56:33,530
God forgive this girl's sins.

895
01:56:34,860 --> 01:56:41,030
If you don't want her to die, you need to
tell us where Edebali's treasure is.

896
01:56:42,090 --> 01:56:47,730
I have a cure that can heal her.

897
01:56:49,020 --> 01:56:54,470
If you give me what I want, I'll let
both of you live.

898
01:56:54,470 --> 01:56:58,910
- So, you'll have forgiven her.
- Who are you?

899
01:56:58,930 --> 01:57:03,280
Monk Yannis, from Margarit Abbey.

900
01:57:41,460 --> 01:57:46,110
My Alps (men) are in the position.
They are waiting for your sign.

901
01:57:46,790 --> 01:57:51,790
If we raid, they will kill both Bala Hatun
and Tursun.

902
01:57:58,650 --> 01:58:03,940
- Son, what are you talking about?
- Bala Hatun and Tursun are inside.

903
01:58:04,730 --> 01:58:10,240
We need to infiltrate so that they don't
get hurt.

904
01:58:24,300 --> 01:58:26,360
Let's go.

905
01:58:45,840 --> 01:58:50,840
Demirbüken, Aykut.
Wait here.

906
01:59:05,920 --> 01:59:10,210
Now, tell me.

907
01:59:10,270 --> 01:59:15,700
What is the reason that made you come
here, Kayı tent?

908
01:59:16,290 --> 01:59:18,970
Justice, Dündar Bey.

909
01:59:19,320 --> 01:59:26,770
So as not to lose contact and damage
our friendship that you built.

910
01:59:27,600 --> 01:59:30,760
This is a friendly visit.

911
01:59:32,650 --> 01:59:40,880
There are several issues damaging
our good relations, Dündar Bey.

912
01:59:41,610 --> 01:59:47,910
That my daughter has been abducted and
brought to your castle is one of them, right?

913
01:59:47,940 --> 01:59:49,960
Of course.

914
01:59:50,430 --> 01:59:54,540
No one would want this to happen.

915
01:59:55,140 --> 02:00:00,980
But, don't forget.
All of this is up to...

916
02:00:01,950 --> 02:00:04,140
Osman.

917
02:00:10,410 --> 02:00:16,530
We intend to solve this problem
without causing any harm, Dündar Bey.

918
02:00:16,710 --> 02:00:25,320
We want to face Osman and ask him our
questions in Alişer Bey's supervision.

919
02:00:27,570 --> 02:00:30,030
This is the best way.

920
02:00:30,430 --> 02:00:36,400
Also, this would hamper the ones who
want to set us against each other.

921
02:00:36,530 --> 02:00:39,020
Call Osman.

922
02:00:46,630 --> 02:00:48,390
Osman is not here.

923
02:00:49,040 --> 02:00:51,420
What do you mean?

924
02:00:53,940 --> 02:00:57,270
They told me that he was in the cage.

925
02:00:58,280 --> 02:01:02,820
He had a problem with Batur.

926
02:01:02,820 --> 02:01:05,640
I commanded to send him into the cage.

927
02:01:07,820 --> 02:01:10,140
But he escaped.

928
02:01:13,770 --> 02:01:18,300
How can't you take care of a criminal...

929
02:01:18,300 --> 02:01:21,590
who is accused of so many crimes,
Gündüz Bey?

930
02:01:24,510 --> 02:01:29,140
How could he escape under all those Alps'
(men) supervision.

931
02:01:29,140 --> 02:01:33,440
Just like how he escaped
from your...

932
02:01:33,440 --> 02:01:38,210
castle's dungeon, in your command,
Kalanoz.

933
02:01:38,400 --> 02:01:42,190
It's obvious you did that before we face
Osman.

934
02:01:42,190 --> 02:01:46,880
Are you playing with us?
This is a reason for war, Dündar Bey!

935
02:01:47,550 --> 02:01:51,550
Kalanoz, when we are born...

936
02:01:51,870 --> 02:01:57,000
before our names,
they whisper "war" into our ears

937
02:01:57,190 --> 02:02:01,800
The one who is afraid of fighting is vile!

938
02:02:22,840 --> 02:02:27,530
How can a monk like you...

939
02:02:27,540 --> 02:02:31,220
so relentless, Yannis?

940
02:02:31,550 --> 02:02:34,320
Let me go, I beg you.

941
02:02:34,320 --> 02:02:36,960
I am Priest Marcus.

942
02:02:37,010 --> 02:02:40,830
You can investigate.

943
02:02:40,830 --> 02:02:45,860
Everyone knows me.
I am Priest Marcus.

944
02:02:52,190 --> 02:02:55,680
Enough, enough.

945
02:02:57,710 --> 02:02:59,660
Megela!

946
02:03:01,810 --> 02:03:05,060
So, you decided to talk.

947
02:03:08,280 --> 02:03:13,090
Kill him, I don't care.

948
02:03:13,700 --> 02:03:18,370
Kill me too.
Let this end.

949
02:03:20,870 --> 02:03:25,890
I don't know where holy entrustment is.

950
02:03:28,580 --> 02:03:33,560
Only my father knows that.

951
02:03:43,690 --> 02:03:46,410
Maybe if you die...

952
02:03:47,840 --> 02:03:50,440
he'll speak.

953
02:03:59,690 --> 02:04:04,310
God, give me strength.

954
02:04:23,200 --> 02:04:25,880
Bala Hatun.

955
02:04:33,600 --> 02:04:36,360
Bala Hatun ha?

956
02:04:39,810 --> 02:04:44,370
Your identity is revealed, priest.

957
02:04:44,880 --> 02:04:48,880
Or should I call you "Edebali's spy"?

958
02:04:48,950 --> 02:04:52,390
You are a devil, Yannis.

959
02:04:53,530 --> 02:04:57,190
We don't know where holy entrustment is.

960
02:04:57,290 --> 02:05:01,290
You can never learn what we don't know.

961
02:05:02,310 --> 02:05:07,900
You can't stop the words of Allah.

962
02:05:08,660 --> 02:05:14,960
You can't stop Turks' awakening and
their foundation.

963
02:05:16,150 --> 02:05:20,380
The wood sword will find its owner.

964
02:05:20,380 --> 02:05:25,110
That day will be your end!

965
02:05:27,700 --> 02:05:30,380
Allah is the greatest!

966
02:05:30,380 --> 02:05:34,820
Allah is the greatest!
Allah is the greatest!

967
02:05:52,660 --> 02:05:55,910
Let's do it son.
It's time.

968
02:05:56,040 --> 02:05:58,160
We are ready, my Bey (chief).

969
02:06:10,190 --> 02:06:12,360
It's a raid!
Raid!

970
02:06:12,360 --> 02:06:15,100
Come on my valiants, get them all!

971
02:06:15,100 --> 02:06:17,520
Allah is eternal!

972
02:07:00,930 --> 02:07:04,600
Sergeant Samsa, Bamsı Bey(chief)
go that way.

973
02:07:11,150 --> 02:07:13,640
Osman is coming!

974
02:07:13,760 --> 02:07:16,420
Osman is coming!

975
02:07:21,280 --> 02:07:23,770
Osman...

976
02:07:24,530 --> 02:07:27,680
- Damn it.
- Sir, what are we going to do?

977
02:07:30,590 --> 02:07:32,820
Osman...

978
02:08:56,680 --> 02:08:58,820
Come with me, Megela.

979
02:09:17,860 --> 02:09:19,540
Bala.

980
02:09:25,320 --> 02:09:27,280
Bala.

981
02:09:45,410 --> 02:09:48,990
Bala, Bala, Bala.

982
02:09:49,470 --> 02:09:50,840
No.

983
02:09:50,900 --> 02:09:54,160
No, no.

984
02:09:54,500 --> 02:09:56,190
Bala.

985
02:09:56,200 --> 02:10:00,260
Bala, bala, open your eyes.
I'm here.

986
02:10:00,720 --> 02:10:03,290
I'm with you.

987
02:10:06,490 --> 02:10:09,960
Tursun, Tursun, Tursun!

988
02:10:13,330 --> 02:10:16,000
Thank Allah, he is alive.

989
02:10:32,270 --> 02:10:37,270
Osman Bey(chief) Edebali's daughter
Bala Hatun...

990
02:10:37,270 --> 02:10:42,680
will die achingly and slowly
in three days.

991
02:10:48,110 --> 02:10:50,830
Only I have her cure.

992
02:10:53,250 --> 02:10:59,050
If you want to save her,
give me what you stole from me back.

993
02:10:59,340 --> 02:11:01,950
Efendi (sir) Yannis.

994
02:11:16,710 --> 02:11:18,520
Bala.

995
02:11:18,620 --> 02:11:20,320
Bala.

996
02:11:21,560 --> 02:11:24,810
Open your eyes, open!

997
02:11:29,100 --> 02:11:31,780
Let your eyes kill me.

998
02:11:32,020 --> 02:11:34,830
Let them destroy me.

999
02:11:37,290 --> 02:11:40,720
I just need you to open your eyes.

1000
02:11:40,760 --> 02:11:42,900
Bala.

1001
02:11:45,310 --> 02:11:46,900
Bala.

1002
02:11:49,620 --> 02:11:51,320
Bala.

1003
02:11:58,820 --> 02:12:01,230
- Osman.
- Bala.

1004
02:12:04,230 --> 02:12:06,910
You came for me.

1005
02:12:08,290 --> 02:12:12,050
Yeah, I came for you.

1006
02:12:12,730 --> 02:12:16,260
I will never leave you again.

1007
02:12:16,520 --> 02:12:20,040
You... know it...

1008
02:12:22,860 --> 02:12:26,210
it is... too late....

1009
02:12:28,760 --> 02:12:33,230
Ya- Yannis' poison... is in my blood.

1010
02:12:44,900 --> 02:12:50,600
I'll find that Yannis even if he
goes to hell.

1011
02:12:51,660 --> 02:12:54,590
I'll come back with your cure.

1012
02:12:59,650 --> 02:13:03,310
Do not do it.

1013
02:13:03,310 --> 02:13:05,610
Don't.

1014
02:13:06,270 --> 02:13:10,710
You... are... hope...

1015
02:13:10,710 --> 02:13:13,650
for... the... people... Osman.

1016
02:13:15,150 --> 02:13:19,200
It's... not.... worth.... for....
a... Bala.

1017
02:13:19,260 --> 02:13:24,000
For a Bala, Kulucahisar aside, ...

1018
02:13:25,170 --> 02:13:27,700
I'd burn the whole universe.

1019
02:13:30,380 --> 02:13:33,280
I'll find your cure and come back.

1020
02:13:33,850 --> 02:13:36,160
Don't give up.

1021
02:13:36,290 --> 02:13:38,520
Think of your father.

1022
02:13:38,760 --> 02:13:41,480
Think of your Ahi (the Ahi Brotherhood)
brothers.

1023
02:13:42,830 --> 02:13:47,720
I'd sacrifice my every breath for you.

1024
02:13:49,310 --> 02:13:51,930
Don't give up.

1025
02:13:53,590 --> 02:13:56,450
Do not give up.

1026
02:13:57,310 --> 02:13:59,340
Give me...

1027
02:14:00,530 --> 02:14:03,070
your... blessings... Osman.

1028
02:14:04,090 --> 02:14:05,540
Bala.

1029
02:14:08,720 --> 02:14:12,030
Bala, Bala, Bala!

1030
02:14:12,090 --> 02:14:15,720
Bala, open your eyes, Bala.

1031
02:14:49,140 --> 02:14:50,910
Thank Allah.

1032
02:14:51,550 --> 02:14:54,160
Thank Allah she is alive.

1033
02:15:03,600 --> 02:15:08,890
When two lovers come together, they
must be happy.

1034
02:15:08,970 --> 02:15:14,060
Be happy.
You are entrusted to Allah.

1035
02:15:14,230 --> 02:15:16,370
Goodbye.

1036
02:15:16,680 --> 02:15:19,030
I didn't like that man.

1037
02:15:19,030 --> 02:15:23,770
Neither the traitors nor the cruels
stop.

1038
02:15:23,790 --> 02:15:27,030
We just need to be honest.

1039
02:15:52,610 --> 02:15:55,790
Find a stretcher for
Bala Hatun and Tursun.

1040
02:15:56,200 --> 02:15:58,870
Take them to my father's tent.

1041
02:16:01,810 --> 02:16:05,410
Bala Hatun is entrusted to my Ayşe Aunt.

1042
02:16:05,510 --> 02:16:08,590
- Do what is necessary.
- Of course, my Bey (chief).

1043
02:16:12,040 --> 02:16:15,660
- They poisoned Bala Hatun.
- Devils.

1044
02:16:15,870 --> 02:16:17,890
They have the cure.

1045
02:16:19,100 --> 02:16:21,720
What do they want, my Bey?

1046
02:16:21,980 --> 02:16:26,090
We are not going to give,
we are going to take!

1047
02:16:28,430 --> 02:16:34,390
Sofia's life in exchange for
Bala Hatun's life!

1048
02:16:34,430 --> 02:17:09,540
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com